+Status: ready for review
+
+## Review finding resolved
+
+Revision 5 was returned because the production validator admitted drift in the
+accepted libssh2 patch and public-header pins. The production call site is
+`scripts/validate-m0-production-bindings.py` through `make m0-bindings-check`.
+It now validates:
+
+- the one checked-in libssh2 patch manifest record and selected patch bytes
+  against accepted `patchSha256`;
+- every required XCFramework slice's checked-in `libssh2.h` lock and actual
+  header bytes against accepted `publicHeaderSha256`;
+- missing, malformed, duplicate, and inconsistent selected SSH pin records at
+  stable failure row `REPOSITORY-SSH-PIN`.
+
+Production-entry negative tests independently mutate the patch lock and one
+required-slice public-header lock. Both require process exit 1 and
+`productionCompositionPermitted=false`.
+
+## Accepted binding and digest evidence
+
+- Repository, owning outcome attachment, and TASK-260715-3ejhyy sole-consumer
+  precondition remain byte-identical at SHA-256
+  `39b3428d6cf778fa6b682bb0853a177d6b85f03b8062309f0d198dcdfd49fae6`.
+- All eight exact M0/M1 accepted outcome and reviewer-verdict resources were
+  independently recomputed and match the immutable manifest.
+- The unchanged authoritative production gate reports no failures and
+  `productionCompositionPermitted=true`; any tested drift reports permission
+  false.
+
+## Validation
+
+- `make m0-bindings-test`: exit 0, 20/20 tests passed.
+- `make m0-bindings-check TASK_BOARD_RESOURCES="$TASK_BOARD_DIR/.resources"`:
+  exit 0, no failures, permission true.
+- `make check-native-dependencies`: exit 0; libssh2 patch, artifact, public API,
+  headers, symbols, and notices verified.
+- Python compile, manifest JSON parse, and `git diff --check`: exit 0.
+- `task-board validate`: process exit 0 while reporting two retained
+  `PARENT_STATUS_MISMATCH` rows (`STORY-260715-1zzt0c` and owning
+  `STORY-260715-1y04r0`). This is recorded as an anomaly, not a clean board.
+
+## Evidence files
