 - REVIEW REWORK 3: CR revision 3 was correctly rejected because raw-source target lookup selected a commented decoy before the real provider declaration. Target and array resolution now use a lexical Swift view: comments cannot supply declarations or fields, string contents cannot supply code candidates, bracket matching ignores both, and duplicate real target declarations fail closed. Production-entry regressions cover the exact comment decoy, a multiline-string decoy, and an ambiguous duplicate target.
 - REVIEW REWORK 4 VALIDATION: The final suite passes 16/16. The unchanged authoritative manifest passes the production Make gate with SHA-256 `39b3428d6cf778fa6b682bb0853a177d6b85f03b8062309f0d198dcdfd49fae6` and permission true; the exact reviewer-attached comment mutant exits 1 at `REPOSITORY-GRAPH` with permission false. Owner and `TASK-260715-3ejhyy` sole-consumer attachments remain byte-identical. `task-board validate` returned process exit 0 while retaining three `PARENT_STATUS_MISMATCH` rows (owning Story stored `to-dev` versus child aggregate `development`, plus two unrelated Stories); the raw result is attached and is not represented as a clean validation.
 - REVIEW REWORK 5: CR revision 4 was correctly rejected because the pinned normalized contract omitted all eight accepted resource digests, allowing changed upstream bytes plus a synchronized mutable-manifest digest to retain permission. The independent canonical trust root now includes every M0 and M1 outcome/verdict SHA-256. The production-entry synchronized-rebind regression refuses at stable row `NORMALIZED-CONTRACT`; the full suite passes 17/17, all eight authoritative digests independently match, and the unchanged owner/repository/sole-consumer manifest remains byte-identical at SHA-256 `39b3428d6cf778fa6b682bb0853a177d6b85f03b8062309f0d198dcdfd49fae6` with permission true.
+- REVIEW REWORK 6: CR revision 5 was correctly rejected because the production gate did not bind the accepted libssh2 patch and public-header SHA-256 values to the checked-in native pin graph. The gate now validates the patch manifest and selected patch bytes plus every required-slice header lock and header bytes; missing, malformed, duplicate, or inconsistent records fail at stable `REPOSITORY-SSH-PIN`. Patch-lock and single-slice header-lock production mutants exit 1 with permission false; the full suite passes 20/20 and the unchanged baseline remains permitted.
 
 ### M0 packet bridge and HEV baseline accepted (TASK-260715-2jatnd)
 
